2300
00:04:16,567 --> 00:04:17,987
An autoreiv?

2301
00:04:18,787 --> 00:04:20,237
She's mechanical.

2302
00:04:21,537 --> 00:04:22,747
A machine...

2303
00:04:25,497 --> 00:04:26,497
Pino!

2304
00:04:27,997 --> 00:04:29,247
Sorry.

2305
00:04:29,247 --> 00:04:31,297
She seems to be shy around strangers.

2306
00:04:31,297 --> 00:04:33,717
She supposedly has the mind of a child,

2307
00:04:33,717 --> 00:04:36,297
but acting like that after you saved her...

2308
00:04:36,757 --> 00:04:38,507
I guess I don't understand her.

2309
00:04:39,887 --> 00:04:42,387
But why did you help us?

2310
00:04:49,397 --> 00:04:52,237
Because you are a friend of mine.

2311
00:04:52,687 --> 00:04:53,607
"Friend"?

2312
00:04:53,897 --> 00:04:57,737
All those who know the ends of the earth are friends.

2313
00:04:58,947 --> 00:05:00,907
"The ends of the earth..."?

2314
00:05:00,907 --> 00:05:05,157
The world you saw, and the world you see.

2315
00:05:05,707 --> 00:05:08,627
Those eyes of yours look upon death.

2316
00:05:09,837 --> 00:05:12,257
That might be true.

2317
00:05:12,257 --> 00:05:14,377
After all, survival...

2318
00:05:14,837 --> 00:05:18,047
will mean seeing much more death.

2319
00:05:18,887 --> 00:05:21,007
My companions died as well.

2320
00:05:21,007 --> 00:05:23,017
I've been alone ever since.

2321
00:05:23,597 --> 00:05:25,307
But why?

2322
00:05:25,307 --> 00:05:27,847
Why was I the one who survived?

2323
00:05:30,857 --> 00:05:32,937
It was fate.

2324
00:05:33,817 --> 00:05:35,857
I'm impressed you've come this far.

2325
00:05:39,317 --> 00:05:41,277
Hop, hop, jump.

2326
00:05:41,577 --> 00:05:43,827
Hop, jump, jump.

2327
00:05:44,997 --> 00:05:46,577
Ow, oww...

2328
00:06:04,717 --> 00:06:07,437
Land of the rising sun, huh.

2329
00:06:08,057 --> 00:06:10,767
It's been a long time since I've seen a view like this.

2330
00:06:13,437 --> 00:06:14,477
Pino.

2331
00:06:14,977 --> 00:06:16,317
What's the matter?

2332
00:06:16,317 --> 00:06:17,527
Take a look.

2333
00:06:17,527 --> 00:06:19,027
It's almost like a maze.

2334
00:06:19,527 --> 00:06:20,487
Hey!

2335
00:06:20,487 --> 00:06:21,697
What's the matter?

2336
00:06:22,197 --> 00:06:22,987
Come!

2337
00:06:22,987 --> 00:06:24,447
What is it?

2338
00:06:26,657 --> 00:06:28,287
What are...

2339
00:06:28,917 --> 00:06:30,037
these?

2340
00:06:39,967 --> 00:06:41,337
Why...

2341
00:06:42,007 --> 00:06:43,137
are they here?

2342
00:06:46,017 --> 00:06:47,307
Let's go back to the ship...

2343
00:06:47,307 --> 00:06:49,017
to the rabbit,

2344
00:06:49,017 --> 00:06:50,187
Vince.

2345
00:06:56,227 --> 00:06:57,357
I don't like this place.

2346
00:06:57,357 --> 00:06:58,777
Let's get out of here.

2347
00:07:03,117 --> 00:07:04,577
I'm scared.

2348
00:07:04,577 --> 00:07:06,327
We can't stay here.

2349
00:07:06,617 --> 00:07:07,827
Let's go together.

2350
00:07:07,827 --> 00:07:08,867
Let's go look for the rabbit.

2351
00:07:10,867 --> 00:07:11,997
Are you just going to sit there?

2352
00:07:11,997 --> 00:07:14,667
I'm going to go alone!

2353
00:07:21,677 --> 00:07:22,797
But...

2354
00:07:22,797 --> 00:07:24,847
he helped me.

2355
00:07:28,177 --> 00:07:29,887
Do you want some too?

2356
00:07:29,887 --> 00:07:31,347
Um, no thank you.

2357
00:07:31,347 --> 00:07:33,517
You haven't touched your food.

2358
00:07:34,517 --> 00:07:36,857
Those autoreivs...

2359
00:07:38,647 --> 00:07:39,607
Oh?

2360
00:07:40,107 --> 00:07:42,907
Oh, you mean the Knights?

2361
00:07:42,907 --> 00:07:45,157
You were at war with Haros?

2362
00:07:45,157 --> 00:07:47,657
You killed many in Haros...

2363
00:07:49,157 --> 00:07:50,407
So?

2364
00:07:53,417 --> 00:07:56,167
Conflict inevitably creates a victor and a loser,

2365
00:07:56,167 --> 00:07:58,167
as well as life and death.

2366
00:07:58,167 --> 00:08:01,757
The conflict wasn't started in ignorance of that.

2367
00:08:01,757 --> 00:08:05,797
But what reason was there to continue attacking Haros?

2368
00:08:05,797 --> 00:08:07,887
Conflict is meaningless.

2369
00:08:07,887 --> 00:08:11,227
However, there is meaning in destruction.

2370
00:08:11,227 --> 00:08:14,097
You saw Haros' end, didn't you?

2371
00:08:15,437 --> 00:08:17,687
You saw Senex, no?

2372
00:08:17,687 --> 00:08:19,317
Senex...

2373
00:08:19,977 --> 00:08:21,817
It destroyed Haros?

2374
00:08:26,487 --> 00:08:28,907
Why are you obsessed with Haros?

2375
00:08:28,907 --> 00:08:31,157
They were in need of purification.

2376
00:08:31,617 --> 00:08:33,537
And that's why you were fighting them?

2377
00:08:33,537 --> 00:08:35,077
Of course not...

2378
00:08:36,247 --> 00:08:41,707
Left behind during the long sleep, they sought meaning.

2379
00:08:42,127 --> 00:08:46,007
To deny the truth of their abandonment...

2380
00:08:46,427 --> 00:08:49,927
they found meaning in seeking each other's destruction.

2381
00:08:50,217 --> 00:08:52,307
The world eventually descended into chaos.

2382
00:08:52,307 --> 00:08:56,977
As their will weakened, even death lost its meaning.

2383
00:08:57,937 --> 00:09:02,607
To think of them as free-willed in the first place

2384
00:09:02,607 --> 00:09:03,987
is simply ludicrous.

2385
00:09:04,897 --> 00:09:07,067
Ill-fated ones...

2386
00:09:10,947 --> 00:09:13,697
No, we should beg forgiveness as well.

2387
00:09:13,697 --> 00:09:15,157
I should,

2388
00:09:15,157 --> 00:09:16,417
as should you.

2389
00:09:16,417 --> 00:09:17,667
I should?

2390
00:09:17,667 --> 00:09:19,667
H-Hey, wait a minute.

2391
00:09:19,667 --> 00:09:21,627
What have I done?

2392
00:09:21,917 --> 00:09:24,757
I've done nothing, and yet I'm always being chased by something.

2393
00:09:24,757 --> 00:09:26,337
Now, I've ended up here.

2394
00:09:26,337 --> 00:09:27,677
That's why, isn't it?

2395
00:09:28,677 --> 00:09:31,347
Not doing anything, not <i>able</i> to do anything.

2396
00:09:31,347 --> 00:09:32,717
It's painful...

2397
00:09:34,427 --> 00:09:36,557
I was that way as well.

2398
00:09:36,557 --> 00:09:37,897
You too?

2399
00:09:37,897 --> 00:09:41,017
I despised myself for not being able to do anything,

2400
00:09:41,017 --> 00:09:44,737
and I was haunted in my sleep

2401
00:09:44,737 --> 00:09:47,277
by the ceaseless verbal abuse from my other self.

2402
00:09:47,277 --> 00:09:49,777
Without meaning, time passed by.

2403
00:09:49,777 --> 00:09:53,037
And to survive that... pain...

2404
00:09:53,697 --> 00:09:57,247
I've felt the same pain you have.

2405
00:09:57,247 --> 00:09:59,127
"The same pain you have"?

2406
00:09:59,457 --> 00:10:01,877
I feel that I could come to love you...

2407
00:10:02,337 --> 00:10:04,707
the way I loved Senex.

2408
00:10:14,307 --> 00:10:17,177
You loved Senex?

2409
00:10:17,177 --> 00:10:19,267
I'll tell you our story.

2410
00:10:20,517 --> 00:10:23,897
If my Asura is the sun, Haros is the moon.

2411
00:10:24,357 --> 00:10:28,817
Senex and I each built a tower that mirrored the other

2412
00:10:28,817 --> 00:10:33,737
as proof of the vows we were to
 exchange on the eventual Day of Awakening.

2413
00:10:33,737 --> 00:10:35,997
Do you understand what I'm talking about?

2414
00:10:36,697 --> 00:10:42,457
Realizing our tragic fate, Senex and I suffered,

2415
00:10:42,457 --> 00:10:44,997
yet also gained love.

2416
00:10:46,257 --> 00:10:50,757
But before we could make those vows, Senex died.

2417
00:10:51,047 --> 00:10:52,717
You killed her.

2418
00:10:53,257 --> 00:10:54,387
No...

2419
00:10:55,257 --> 00:10:56,467
But that's fine.

2420
00:10:56,467 --> 00:10:59,437
Before fate, vows are but fragile things.

2421
00:11:00,017 --> 00:11:03,727
Instead, I think it fortunate that I was able to meet you.

2422
00:11:04,477 --> 00:11:06,777
I thank your strength.

2423
00:11:08,147 --> 00:11:10,647
What are you saying?

2424
00:11:10,647 --> 00:11:11,777
What?

2425
00:11:11,777 --> 00:11:13,487
<i>I</i> killed her?

2426
00:11:13,487 --> 00:11:14,697
Her?

2427
00:11:14,697 --> 00:11:17,077
How could I have?

2428
00:11:17,077 --> 00:11:18,037
What are you saying?

2429
00:11:18,037 --> 00:11:19,037
Senex was-

2430
00:11:19,037 --> 00:11:20,537
Please stop!

2431
00:11:20,537 --> 00:11:21,577
You are...

2432
00:11:21,577 --> 00:11:23,537
I don't know anything!

2433
00:11:23,537 --> 00:11:25,377
You're joking with me, aren't you?

2434
00:11:25,377 --> 00:11:26,417
Aren't you?

2435
00:11:26,417 --> 00:11:29,257
What does she have anything to do with <i>me</i>?

2436
00:11:29,257 --> 00:11:30,667
Please.

2437
00:11:30,667 --> 00:11:32,587
Tell me it's true.

2438
00:11:33,217 --> 00:11:35,047
What are you?

2439
00:11:35,507 --> 00:11:36,927
You...

2440
00:11:36,927 --> 00:11:39,597
are supposed to suffer as I do.

2441
00:11:36,927 --> 00:11:40,177
Are you going to make me suffer?

2442
00:11:40,177 --> 00:11:41,187
Why?

2443
00:11:41,187 --> 00:11:43,307
I don't know anything!

2444
00:11:47,227 --> 00:11:48,937
Has he lost his memories?!

2445
00:12:04,957 --> 00:12:07,287
He killed, unknowing?

2446
00:12:07,287 --> 00:12:09,457
He killed my Senex.

2447
00:12:46,327 --> 00:12:47,627
Why...

2448
00:12:47,627 --> 00:12:50,747
This is my Asura's true appearance.

2449
00:12:51,757 --> 00:12:54,047
You saw this, didn't you?

2450
00:12:55,757 --> 00:12:58,137
It's just a monument.

2451
00:12:58,137 --> 00:13:01,717
Asura's residents must've made it

2452
00:13:01,717 --> 00:13:04,137
to record Asura's former glory for posterity,

2453
00:13:04,597 --> 00:13:06,267
but it was useless.

2454
00:13:06,267 --> 00:13:08,107
What happened to Asura's residents?

2455
00:13:08,107 --> 00:13:09,687
They all perished.

2456
00:13:09,687 --> 00:13:12,147
They were destroyed by the Knights.

2457
00:13:12,147 --> 00:13:13,527
What?!

2458
00:13:13,527 --> 00:13:16,107
Haros and Asura were one.

2459
00:13:16,107 --> 00:13:20,367
Their residents died due to conflict, and only the Knights remained.

2460
00:13:20,367 --> 00:13:21,537
Then...

2461
00:13:21,537 --> 00:13:23,367
Haros' soldiers were...

2462
00:13:23,867 --> 00:13:26,077
They were a lie.

2463
00:13:26,077 --> 00:13:29,667
Merely a lie returned to nothingness by death.

2464
00:13:29,667 --> 00:13:30,497
But...

2465
00:13:30,497 --> 00:13:32,297
they were alive!

2466
00:13:33,457 --> 00:13:36,757
Once alive, people have no choice but to continue living.

2467
00:13:36,757 --> 00:13:38,257
"People", hm?

2468
00:13:38,257 --> 00:13:42,887
Right now, I am happy, for all life has ended.

2469
00:13:42,887 --> 00:13:44,057
Why?

2470
00:13:44,057 --> 00:13:46,267
Aren't you their master?

2471
00:13:47,977 --> 00:13:50,307
You are a fool.

2472
00:13:50,807 --> 00:13:54,487
Having lost your memories, have
 you also lost the ability to see the truth?

2473
00:13:54,487 --> 00:13:56,027
I <i>have</i> my memories!

2474
00:13:56,027 --> 00:13:57,987
Then who are you?

2475
00:13:58,907 --> 00:14:01,407
Try telling me who you are.

2476
00:14:01,907 --> 00:14:04,077
I am Vincent Law.

2477
00:14:04,077 --> 00:14:06,957
I was working in Romdeau's Control Division.

2478
00:14:06,957 --> 00:14:09,117
but I was placed under suspicion of treason,

2479
00:14:09,117 --> 00:14:10,917
and fled from the dome.

2480
00:14:10,917 --> 00:14:12,417
And before that?

2481
00:14:12,417 --> 00:14:13,997
I was in the Mosk dome.

2482
00:14:13,997 --> 00:14:15,547
I was an immigrant.

2483
00:14:15,547 --> 00:14:17,417
What were you doing in Mosk?

2484
00:14:17,417 --> 00:14:18,467
What was I doing?

2485
00:14:20,927 --> 00:14:22,927
You don't remember, do you?

2486
00:14:23,717 --> 00:14:28,267
Despite your vague memories, you've
 managed to live without any doubts until now.

2487
00:14:28,937 --> 00:14:34,527
Isn't that definitive proof that you
 deliberately erased your own memories?

2488
00:14:34,527 --> 00:14:36,107
Erased memories?

2489
00:14:36,107 --> 00:14:38,237
You said you were in Mosk, no?

2490
00:14:38,237 --> 00:14:39,027
Yes.

2491
00:14:39,027 --> 00:14:40,447
It is my homeland.

2492
00:14:40,447 --> 00:14:41,867
I see.

2493
00:14:41,867 --> 00:14:43,697
It was Monad, wasn't it.

2494
00:14:43,697 --> 00:14:46,657
You gave him your memories, didn't you.

2495
00:14:46,657 --> 00:14:50,747
But when you absorb another's memories,
 you're unable to bear their sheer volume.

2496
00:14:51,417 --> 00:14:53,917
Even so, he accepted them.

2497
00:14:54,207 --> 00:14:55,877
He must have loved you.

2498
00:14:57,967 --> 00:15:02,177
But by showing you his love, Monad lost you.

2499
00:15:02,177 --> 00:15:04,557
No, not just Monad...

2500
00:15:04,557 --> 00:15:06,717
You also lost yourself.

2501
00:15:07,267 --> 00:15:14,227
To erase your memories is to lose the very essence of who you are.

2502
00:15:14,227 --> 00:15:16,477
What are you talking about?

2503
00:15:16,937 --> 00:15:19,737
I'm saying that you are a traitor.

2504
00:15:19,737 --> 00:15:21,027
A traitor?

2505
00:15:21,027 --> 00:15:22,237
Since when?

2506
00:15:22,737 --> 00:15:24,117
You fled...

2507
00:15:24,117 --> 00:15:27,737
in a way that brings utmost shame to a PROXY.

2508
00:15:27,737 --> 00:15:29,157
"PROXY"?

2509
00:15:29,497 --> 00:15:31,827
But what I find even more unforgivable...

2510
00:15:32,327 --> 00:15:34,127
is that without your memories,

2511
00:15:34,127 --> 00:15:38,167
you killed my beloved Senex!

2512
00:15:44,087 --> 00:15:46,677
I am the proxy of brilliance,

2513
00:15:47,007 --> 00:15:49,017
Kazkis PROXY.

2514
00:15:49,477 --> 00:15:53,977
I swear on my honor that I will eliminate the traitor.

2515
00:16:19,047 --> 00:16:20,377
What's the matter?

2516
00:16:20,377 --> 00:16:22,587
Even after erasing your memory and losing your self,

2517
00:16:22,587 --> 00:16:24,927
you still have your instincts, don't you?

2518
00:16:24,927 --> 00:16:29,347
Thinking that, I find those who live on
 the path of insanity all the more endearing!

2519
00:16:29,347 --> 00:16:30,597
Senex...

2520
00:16:30,597 --> 00:16:35,267
I'll go insane as well, with my memories of having lived with you!

2521
00:16:36,937 --> 00:16:38,647
Sorry, sorry...

2522
00:16:38,647 --> 00:16:40,277
Did that hurt?

2523
00:16:53,707 --> 00:16:54,367
Hop, hop, hop!

2524
00:16:54,367 --> 00:16:55,037
Hop, hop, hop!

2525
00:16:55,037 --> 00:16:55,827
Hop, hop, hop!

2526
00:16:55,827 --> 00:16:56,707
Rabbit!

2527
00:17:34,287 --> 00:17:36,037
What is... this?

2528
00:17:38,577 --> 00:17:39,837
My arm!

2529
00:17:50,717 --> 00:17:52,137
Help me!

2530
00:17:52,637 --> 00:17:53,807
It hurts!

2531
00:17:57,267 --> 00:17:59,097
Am I a monster?

2532
00:17:59,097 --> 00:18:00,107
No...

2533
00:18:00,107 --> 00:18:01,317
I am...

2534
00:18:02,017 --> 00:18:04,737
You are a PROXY.

2535
00:18:06,027 --> 00:18:07,357
"PROXY"?

2536
00:18:08,527 --> 00:18:11,447
I wonder what this feeling is...

2537
00:18:12,527 --> 00:18:14,577
You disgust me...

2538
00:18:14,577 --> 00:18:16,617
I feel as though I may vomit.

2539
00:18:16,617 --> 00:18:18,787
Yes, that's right...

2540
00:18:18,787 --> 00:18:19,997
You...

2541
00:18:19,997 --> 00:18:22,287
<i>You...</i>

2542
00:18:23,337 --> 00:18:25,757
I'll let you name yourself for the last time.

2543
00:18:25,757 --> 00:18:28,177
What are you the proxy of?

2544
00:18:30,257 --> 00:18:32,007
You cannot answer?

2545
00:18:32,547 --> 00:18:35,347
Then die!

2546
00:18:37,807 --> 00:18:39,387
Flee!

2547
00:18:39,387 --> 00:18:41,267
But you are already within a trap!

2548
00:18:41,267 --> 00:18:43,817
Both you... and I!

2549
00:18:44,397 --> 00:18:46,187
Ninety-eight rabbits.

2550
00:18:46,187 --> 00:18:47,937
Ninety-nine rabbits.

2551
00:18:47,937 --> 00:18:49,907
One hundred rabbits!

2552
00:18:50,657 --> 00:18:51,657
Okay!

2553
00:18:51,657 --> 00:18:54,827
I already counted to one hundred, so
 I'm going to leave Vince behind, okay?

2554
00:19:00,167 --> 00:19:01,327
Fifty more!

2555
00:19:01,997 --> 00:19:03,747
One hundred and one rabbits!

2556
00:19:04,377 --> 00:19:05,957
One hundred and two rabbits!

2557
00:19:06,837 --> 00:19:08,297
One hundred and three rabbits!

2558
00:19:26,727 --> 00:19:28,147
This is worthless.

2559
00:19:28,687 --> 00:19:30,897
It lacks fragrance.

2560
00:19:30,897 --> 00:19:32,607
This one is also worthless.

2561
00:19:32,607 --> 00:19:34,907
Too acidic; low class.

2562
00:19:34,907 --> 00:19:37,577
There are no good ones left...

2563
00:19:37,577 --> 00:19:39,957
only rejects.

2564
00:19:39,957 --> 00:19:41,457
Please tell me.

2565
00:19:41,457 --> 00:19:43,497
What are the PROXY?

2566
00:19:43,957 --> 00:19:47,627
Why are you asking, after erasing your own memories?

2567
00:19:48,047 --> 00:19:50,717
Am I a PROXY?

2568
00:19:51,507 --> 00:19:53,927
Why must I fight?

2569
00:19:54,387 --> 00:19:56,467
Then why did you come back?

2570
00:19:56,467 --> 00:19:58,887
You wish to kill me, don't you?

2571
00:19:58,887 --> 00:19:59,977
No.

2572
00:19:59,977 --> 00:20:01,977
Time has awakened.

2573
00:20:01,977 --> 00:20:04,347
I don't want to harm anyone!

2574
00:20:04,347 --> 00:20:05,307
Then...

2575
00:20:05,307 --> 00:20:07,357
who killed Senex?

2576
00:20:08,107 --> 00:20:10,817
Was Senex the only one you killed?

2577
00:20:24,417 --> 00:20:30,337
You've lost both your mission and your
 loved one, so why do you still try to live?

2578
00:20:30,337 --> 00:20:32,507
Why don't you die here?

2579
00:20:37,257 --> 00:20:38,887
Senex...

2580
00:20:38,887 --> 00:20:41,677
I would've liked to have seen you again in life.

2581
00:20:41,677 --> 00:20:45,597
I shall avenge your death.

2582
00:21:15,837 --> 00:21:17,137
I did not...

2583
00:21:17,137 --> 00:21:18,547
wish this...

2584
00:21:19,007 --> 00:21:20,217
Why...?

2585
00:21:20,887 --> 00:21:22,427
I ask you...

2586
00:21:22,717 --> 00:21:23,767
once again...

2587
00:21:23,767 --> 00:21:26,937
what are you the proxy of?

2588
00:21:31,477 --> 00:21:32,977
My name is...

2589
00:21:32,977 --> 00:21:34,947
Ergo PROXY...

2590
00:21:35,527 --> 00:21:37,987
the proxy of death.

2591
00:21:38,817 --> 00:21:40,447
I see.

2592
00:21:44,247 --> 00:21:46,207
May you suffer.

2593
00:21:46,207 --> 00:21:48,707
All those who wander the darkness

2594
00:21:48,707 --> 00:21:50,457
seek the light.

2595
00:21:50,997 --> 00:21:53,417
But when you reach the light...

2596
00:21:53,957 --> 00:21:56,087
you avert your eyes from the brilliance.

2597
00:21:56,547 --> 00:21:58,507
You even feel pain.

2598
00:21:58,507 --> 00:22:00,887
It is the same with truth.

2599
00:22:00,887 --> 00:22:05,557
One day, your eyes will be scorched by the light that is truth,

2600
00:22:05,557 --> 00:22:07,727
and know eternal darkness.

2601
00:22:08,017 --> 00:22:09,977
That is your judgment!

2602
00:22:23,867 --> 00:22:25,907
Senex...

2603
00:22:35,837 --> 00:22:38,297
<i>Am I not human?</i>

2604
00:22:39,007 --> 00:22:39,797
<i>Then...</i>

2605
00:22:41,507 --> 00:22:43,047
<i>how am I to live?</i>

2606
00:22:45,307 --> 00:22:46,767
Four hundred...

2607
00:22:46,767 --> 00:22:48,477
rabbits...

2608
00:22:55,647 --> 00:22:56,937
Vince!

2609
00:22:57,647 --> 00:22:58,817
Pino...

2610
00:22:58,817 --> 00:23:00,157
Did you get hurt?

2611
00:23:00,157 --> 00:23:01,157
No...

2612
00:23:03,907 --> 00:23:05,867
No, it's not my blood.

2613
00:23:05,867 --> 00:23:08,157
Oh, it's the other one...

2614
00:23:09,957 --> 00:23:12,917
The other Vince, the one who's not you.

2615
00:23:13,747 --> 00:23:14,957
Welcome back!

2616
00:23:17,007 --> 00:23:18,337
You...

2617
00:23:18,337 --> 00:23:19,717
knew?

2618
00:23:27,427 --> 00:23:29,427
Let's go to Mosk.

2619
00:23:37,727 --> 00:23:39,397
Weren't you afraid?

2620
00:23:39,397 --> 00:23:40,487
Of me?

2621
00:23:40,487 --> 00:23:41,697
Afraid?

2622
00:23:41,987 --> 00:23:44,317
But you always save me.

2623
00:23:44,987 --> 00:23:46,197
I see.

2624
00:23:48,077 --> 00:23:50,157
<i>Although I can't see anything,</i>

2625
00:23:50,157 --> 00:23:52,077
<i>I've begun to move...</i>

2626
00:23:52,787 --> 00:23:56,087
<i>from the moment the two of us leapt out of Romdeau.</i>

